+  // iOS 26 throws "_presentViewController inside _runAlongsideCompletions" -> SIGABRT
+  // when presentViewController: is called while ANY view controller in the presenter's
+  // hierarchy has an active transitionCoordinator. iOS 26 registers the call as an alongside
+  // completion block; when the coordinator's transition ends, that block fires inside
+  // _runAlongsideCompletions and crashes.
+  //
+  // A single dispatch_async only delays one run-loop cycle (~16ms); active transitions
+  // run for ~350ms. We must keep deferring until every coordinator on the presenter chain
+  // (and on the topmost presented VC) is clear, then call presentViewController: in a clean
+  // run-loop tick that is past _runAlongsideCompletions.
